    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.misc\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.13 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nHello, \n\nI think I may have found a small conflict with the internal :restart command and the mini.misc.setup_auto_root(). When you attempt to restart with this not being differed with something like vim.schedule. It will change the root but this means that restart does not work as intended. \n\n```lua\n-if package.loaded[\"mini.misc\"] then\n-       misc.setup_auto_root()\n-end\n+       -- Deferred to avoid conflicts with :restart process handover\n+       vim.schedule(function()\n+               if package.loaded[\"mini.misc\"] then\n+                       misc.setup_auto_root()\n+               end\n+       end)\n```\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```lua\n-- repro_restart.lua\n-- 1. Manually add mini.nvim to the package path\npackage.path = package.path .. \";/home/[USER]/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/?.lua\"\n\n-- 2. Safe_require to match my config.\n_G.Config = {\n\tsafe_require = function(mod)\n\t\tlocal ok, res = pcall(require, mod)\n\t\treturn ok and res or nil\n\tend,\n}\n\n-- 3. Basic options\nvim.opt.laststatus = 3\n\n-- 4. Load mini.misc\nlocal mini_misc = require(\"mini.misc\")\nmini_misc.setup()\n\n-- 5. THE CULPRIT: Immediate auto_root setup\n-- This attaches PWD-shifting logic to BufEnter/VimEnter.\n-- This was solved with the wrapping of a vim.schedule()\nmini_misc.setup_auto_root()\n\nprint(\"--- REPRODUCER ACTIVE ---\")\nprint(\"PWD: \" .. vim.fn.getcwd())\nprint(\"Execute :restart and observe the blank screen / PWD shift.\")\n```",
