            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@abeldekat Ah thanks for the update I didn't know that. I will be sure to check minimax next time.\n\n@echasnovski yeah to clarify I mean when I restart I expect to reopen the buffer that I initially restarted on. But when I restart with the auto_root. I will change my root to the git root and will give me either a empty buffer with the name of the file I was on or will reopen a blank nvim. See screenshots below:\n\n## No vim.schedule()\n\n<img width=\"800\" height=\"450\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ae7e4fe7-6df1-4d62-8d43-5ef65b2cbc14\" />\n\n## After vim.schedule()\n\nAlso, after testing more I noticed the issue isn't completely gone with after the vim.schedule()\n\nIt doesn't seem to cause an issue as long as I don't bring up mini,files, see below:\n\n<img width=\"800\" height=\"450\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/924f6c7b-42f6-4494-8a14-9c8a4d6abc42\" />",
