        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> [@echasnovski](https://github.com/echasnovski) yeah to clarify I mean when I restart I expect to reopen the buffer that I initially restarted on. But when I restart with the auto_root. I will change my root to the git root and will give me either a empty buffer with the name of the file I was on or will reopen a blank nvim. See screenshots below:\n\nCan you please clarify a bit more about \"expect to reopen the buffer that I initially restarted on\"? What does `nfzf` do? Is this equivalent of `nvim relative/path/to/file` where the file path is pre-selected with `fzf`? If yes, then this is the same issue as described in neovim/neovim#39239 and it can be reproduced without `setup_auto_root()` by manually calling `:cd ..` (i.e. changing Neovim's working directory).\n\nNow, theoretically, this can be attempted to be fixed on the `setup_auto_root` side with something like restoring original cwd on `VimLeavePre`. But 1) I am not sure if that will be without other unwanted side effects; 2) this is how `:restart` currently works and will probably change in the (hopefully near) future.\n\nAnd in the meantime, `restart()` from 'mini.sessions' will work as expected here.",
