        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> > [@echasnovski](https://github.com/echasnovski) yeah to clarify I mean when I restart I expect to reopen the buffer that I initially restarted on. But when I restart with the auto_root. I will change my root to the git root and will give me either a empty buffer with the name of the file I was on or will reopen a blank nvim. See screenshots below:\n> \n> Can you please clarify a bit more about \"expect to reopen the buffer that I initially restarted on\"? What does `nfzf` do? Is this equivalent of `nvim relative/path/to/file` where the file path is pre-selected with `fzf`? If yes, then this is the same issue as described in [neovim/neovim#39239](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/39239) and it can be reproduced without `setup_auto_root()` by manually calling `:cd ..` (i.e. changing Neovim's working directory).\n\nYes it is as you explained `nfzf` is `nvim relative/path/to/file` I didn't think about the confusion it could cause my bad. And yeah from what I understand it is that upstream issue you mentioned and I will have to map out the mini.sessions restart. Thank you for your time.",
